; The MCP server process. It is the only executable that links [writ_mcp], and
; the only file in the MCP tree allowed to perform I/O — the read/write loop
; lives here so every module it drives stays a function from values to values.

; Installed alongside `writ` as `writ-mcp`, so a machine that only ran
; `opam install writ` can point an MCP client at it with nothing else to fetch.

; ONE module on purpose. Dune wraps a multi-module executable as
; [Dune__exe__…], and this exe's main module has the same name as the library
; it links — so a second module here turns [Writ_mcp.Server] into an alias for
; the executable itself and the build stops. The generated [Version] therefore
; lives in the library next door, not beside this file.

(executable
 (name writ_mcp)
 (public_name writ-mcp)
 (package writ)
 (modules writ_mcp)
 (libraries writ_data writ_syntax writ_runtime writ_mcp writ_json writ_loadpath))
